    "rescue_therapy_rules": {
      "value": "If medically necessary (i.e., to control intolerable AD symptoms), rescue treatment for AD may be provided at investigator discretion. Investigators should limit the first step of rescue to topical medications (higher-potency TCS: EU Class >3 / US Class <4), escalating to systemic medications only after at least 14 days without adequate response; subjects on topical rescue continue IMP. Systemic corticosteroid/immunosuppressive rescue requires immediate IMP discontinuation; IMP may resume no sooner than 5 half-lives after the last dose of systemic rescue medication.",
